▪ All-Dings-Ideas

▪▪ Identity, History And Historical Universes

These Ideas preserve a long-term Direction without extending the executable
V30 Scope. A Dings keeps one stable Identity across Files, Representations,
Backends and historical States.

▪▪▪ Native Dings History

Every successfully materialized Commit may later become an immutable normal
Dings with its own Dings Number. Parent Relations and
❲Dings_SM_Patch❳❪300043939.md❫ describe History without making a Git Hash the
public Identity. Amend, Rebase, Cherry-Pick or another Content or Parent Change
creates a new Commit-Dings. Git remains a possible Adapter rather than a
required Backend.

The detailed future Work is recorded in
❲Establish-Native-Dings-Commit-and-History-Model❳❪300101016.md❫.

▪▪▪ Dings Versions And Manifestations

A normal historical View is one stable Dings Identity resolved inside one
immutable Universe Revision. It is not automatically a new Dings. A selected
View becomes an independently numbered ‵Dings_Version‵ only when it is
explicitly materialized for Citation, Publication, Signing, Archiving,
Embedding or independent Claims.

Authored Source, canonical SM, semantic Media Composition, byte-exact Source
and rendered Output remain distinct Projections with distinct Integrity and
Equality Contracts.

The detailed future Work is recorded in
❲Establish-Dings-Version-and-Manifestation-Model❳❪300101017.md❫.

▪▪▪ Chunked Big-Data

The existing ‵.Big-Data‵ Direction may later store large immutable Payloads as
content-addressed Chunks. Dings_SM describes Structure, Meaning, Order and
Composition while multiple Dings Versions reuse unchanged Chunks.

Media Chunking should understand Container, Track, Fragment and GOP Structure,
use content-defined Chunking inside large opaque Regions and preserve a
byte-oriented Fallback. Canonical semantic Media, byte-exact Source Assembly
and rendered Manifestations remain separate. A technical Chunk becomes a
normal Dings only when it needs independent Meaning or Claims.

Publication verifies the complete required Payload Closure before a new Head
becomes visible. Reachability and Retention protect every Chunk needed by a
published Version or Universe Snapshot.

The detailed future Work is recorded in
❲Establish-Chunked-Big-Data-Storage❳❪300101018.md❫.

▪▪▪ Dings Universe Revisions And Wayback

Wayback enters a consistent historical State of the complete Dings Universe,
not merely an old View of one Dings. Every published World State is an
immutable Universe Revision. Every Resolve, Query, Build, Render, Link,
Embedding, Name, Claim, Media and Payload Lookup inherits that ambient Context.

If a referenced Dings did not yet exist, the historical Resolver reports that
Fact instead of falling back to its current View. A Time Expression selects a
Universe Revision; the Revision is the stable Context. A materialized, named,
pinned or citable Revision may become a numbered ‵Dings_Universe_Snapshot‵.

A Universe Revision pins the participating Repository, Configuration, Build
and ‵.Big-Data‵ States as one verified Vector. This prevents a synthetic
Combination of independently selected Repository States that never existed as
one published Dings World.

The detailed future Work is recorded in
❲Establish-Dings-Universe-Revisions-and-Wayback❳❪300101019.md❫.

▪▪▪ V30 Boundary

V30 implements none of these future Runtime Models. It introduces no native
Commit-Dings, Version Engine, chunked Big-Data Store, Universe Revision,
Wayback Surface, Retention Runtime or private Git Workflow Store. The active
V30 Work remains focused on general Work Query, State-Machine and Manifest
Mutation Primitives.

▪▪ Apps

▪▪▪ General

◦ Search Apps for Referenes and provide it to ❲Navigator❳❪300040011.md❫.
◦ Allow Anchors in ❲Image_Maps❳❪300040008.md❫ and Videos
◦ Automatically generate Timelines.

▪▪▪ Media Content Addressing And Claims

◦ Address observable Media Content not only through spatial Image Regions,
  but also through a local Movie or Audio Playback Position and Time Range.
◦ Keep Source Asset, Address Space, Position or Range, observed Content,
  Observer, Evidence and provenance separate from the interpreted Claim.
◦ Distinguish a Song that is playing at one Position from a Song that begins
  there or occupies one complete Interval.
◦ Use an explicit ❲Dings_Channel_Address❳❪300045005.md❫ or
  ❲Dings_Channel_Range❳❪300045006.md❫ in the Playback-Time Address Space
  instead of treating a local Position such as ‵01:44:53‵ as absolute BCT.
◦ Later derive mapping-controlled Claims without adding an unsupported ‵@‵
  Suffix to the current MD Manifest Grammar.

▪▪▪▪ Dog Food

❲Masters-of-the-Universe-2026-Movie❳❪200040071.md❫ records
❲Princes-of-the-Universe-Song❳❪91000031.md❫ as a global Song Relation.
Its authored DMD Observation states that the Song is playing in the local Movie
Playback Range ‵01:44:53-01:46:48‵. The Range is measured from the beginning
of the Movie Playback Timeline and does not yet identify corresponding
Positions within the Song's own Timeline.

Until context-bound Statement and Observation Semantics are executable, the
valid MD Relation and parser-safe DMD Observation preserve both Pieces without
inventing a typed Meaning. This is temporal Media-Content Dog Food for
❲Media-Content-vs-Claims❳❪300100143.md❫.

